# Patch version on commit

Every commit must include a patch bump of `package.json` (and `package-lock.json`).

- A git `pre-commit` hook (`.githooks/pre-commit`) runs `npm version patch --no-git-tag-version` and stages the result. Do not bypass it (`--no-verify` is banned).
- Before `git commit` / `git push`, rely on that hook — do not manually bump unless the hook is missing; if missing, run `node scripts/install-git-hooks.mjs` then commit again.
- To skip a bump for a rare exception: `SKIP_VERSION_BUMP=1 git commit ...` (only if the user explicitly asks).
- Do not create git tags for these patch bumps unless the user asks.
